// Scene: material-text-styles — generated from `ui-libraries/material/parity/scenes/material-text-styles.json`
// (edit the scene, regenerate with `cargo run -p material-parity-generator`).
//PARITY=xfail: Compose keeps text at its natural font metrics — the node bounds stay asc+desc and the baseline sits at the natural ascent regardless of lineHeight — while slint's `line-height` hard-sets the line box and parley splits the leading half above/half below, so element h differs by the lineHeight-vs-natural gap and glyph ink lands ~1-3px off vertically inside its cells. Parley also appends letter-spacing after the trailing cluster (+up to one tracking unit of advance vs Compose).
//SIZE=640x540
//TRACE_ELEMENTS=text0,text1,text2,text3,text4,text5,text6,text7,text8,text9,text10,text11,text12,text13,text14,text15,text16,text17,text18,text19,text20,text21,text22,text23,text24,text25,text26,text27,text28,text29
